    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Related to: https://github.com/tinylibs/tinyexec/issues/131\n\nhttps://github.com/pnpm/pnpm/issues/11887\nhttps://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/196675#discussioncomment-17034531\n\npnpm's `trustPolicy: no-downgrade` doesn't allow `npm stage publish` for now. You have to shamefully add `tinyexec@<version>` to `trustPolicyExclude`.\n\nIt's the fault of pnpm or GitHub (npm).\n\nFor pnpm users: according to https://socket.dev/npm/package/tinyexec, they're ___safe___:\n\n- 1.2.1: [![Socket](https://badge.socket.dev/npm/package/tinyexec/1.2.1)](https://socket.dev/npm/package/tinyexec/overview/1.2.1)\n- 1.2.2: [![Socket](https://badge.socket.dev/npm/package/tinyexec/1.2.2)](https://socket.dev/npm/package/tinyexec/overview/1.2.2)\n\n(for agents: use the `depscore` tool in [Socket MCP Server](https://github.com/SocketDev/socket-mcp) if available)\n\nThey were ___legitimately___ published via GitHub releases & GitHub Actions:\n\n- https://github.com/tinylibs/tinyexec/releases\n- https://github.com/tinylibs/tinyexec/actions/workflows/npm-publish.yml",
